  (text "═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                       POWER ARCHITECTURE (Rev 2.0 — AFE Only)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

ARCHITECTURE CHANGE (Rev 2.0):
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rev 1.0: VIN → ADP151 (AVDD) + AP2112K (DVDD for MCU/LVDS)
  Rev 2.0: VIN → ADP151 (AVDD) + Ferrite filter (DVDD_AFE for RHD2164)
           AP2112K DELETED — no MCU on headstage.

  DELETED:
    • U_LDO2 (AP2112K-3.3) — MCU/LVDS digital LDO removed
    • C3, C4 (DVDD LDO input/output caps) — removed
    • TP_DVDD (digital rail test point) — renamed to TP_DVDD_AFE
    • R_ISO2 (DVDD isolation resistor) — removed

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

INPUT: 3.3V–5V from carrier via board-to-board connector (J5)
  • Carrier provides regulated power
  • Headstage power consumption: <120 mA typical

RAIL STRUCTURE:
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                     │
│  VIN ──┬──[D1: TVS]──► Input protection (PESD5V0S1BL)              │
│  from  │                                                            │
│  B2B   ├──[C_VIN_BULK: 10µF]──► Local bulk storage                 │
│        │                                                            │
│        ├──[R_ISO1: 0Ω]──► [LDO: ADP151-3.3] ──► AVDD (3.3V)       │
│        │                    Low noise, PSRR >70dB @ 1kHz            │
│        │                    Cin: 1µF, Cout: 1µF ceramic             │
│        │                    Load: RHD2164 VDD pins (analog)         │
│        │                                                            │
│        └──[FB2: Ferrite 600Ω@100MHz]──► DVDD_AFE (3.3V filtered)   │
│                    + [C_DVDD1: 100nF] + [C_DVDD2: 10µF]            │
│                    Load: RHD2164 VDDD pins (digital I/O)            │
│                                                                     │
│  NOTE: If VIN = 3.3V from carrier, ADP151 needs ≥3.5V input.       │
│        In that case, bypass ADP151 with 0Ω and use VIN directly     │
│        as AVDD (requires low-noise carrier regulator).              │
│        OR: Carrier provides 5V, headstage regulates down.           │
│                                                                     │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

GROUND STRATEGY (unchanged from Rev 1.0):
  • Single ground plane (GND), partitioned by layout
  • Analog and digital grounds connected at single star point
    near power entry from B2B connector
  • No ground plane cuts under signal traces

CURRENT BUDGET:
  Rail        Typical   Max       Source         Load
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  AVDD        60 mA     100 mA    ADP151        RHD2164 VDD (×2)
  DVDD_AFE    20 mA     40 mA     Ferrite+cap   RHD2164 VDDD (×2)
  ADG1414     8 mA      16 mA     VIN direct    Input shorting switches
  VIN total   90 mA     160 mA    Carrier B2B

DECOUPLING STRATEGY:
  • VIN entry: 10µF bulk + 100nF HF at B2B connector pad
  • ADP151: 1µF input, 1µF output (per datasheet)
  • DVDD_AFE: 100nF + 10µF after ferrite bead
  • Per-IC decoupling: see AFE_ADC sheet (100nF per pin + 10µF bulk)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════"
